From b547a322f10da1f44bb308d6ca9d7cadd7582e49 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: folia-mobile <mobile@folia.local>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 11:19:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 09/21] feat(netease): answer the NetEase API routes inside the
 shell, with no server

The app talks to a NetEase API instance over plain JSON: that instance is what
runs the eapi/weapi encryption and keeps the session. A phone has no instance,
so those routes are now answered locally instead of the feature being dead.

Route shapes are copied from the instance's own modules and checked against what
services/netease.ts reads back, because a wrong shape does not raise - it just
leaves the QR screen waiting forever.

Scope: QR login, login status, search, song detail, playback URL, lyrics,
playlists, daily recommendations, personal FM, likes, chorus. Everything else
answers the instance's own 'route not found' JSON, so the existing degradation
paths keep working unchanged. Listening reports (scrobble/v1) are NOT
implemented - they need the NCBL log upload, and a fake 200 would claim a play
that no server accepted.

Three things are deliberately conservative, because the cost of being wrong here
is a flagged account rather than a visible bug:

- The guest-token bootstrap is throttled to one attempt per ten minutes, kept in
  storage so a reload does not re-hammer it. Retrying on every request would
  double the traffic exactly when a failure suggests something is already
  looking.
- An explicitly configured instance address still wins, so nobody's existing
  setup silently changes backend.
- The QR image is drawn locally (the instance only builds a URL too), and
  playback URLs are forced to https because http audio would be blocked as
  mixed content on this origin.

Whether NetEase's anti-bot accepts this is unproven on a device. The package
ships xeapi/neapi for exactly that reason; if this gets refused, do not paper
over it here.
